-- THEOREM 1D (Universal 4x4 Even/Odd Block Determinant & Trace Identity):
-- For ANY 4x4 tridiagonal Q_real with off-diagonals (a1, a2, a3), Q^2 decouples strictly into:
--   Even block {0, 2}: [[a1^2, -a1*a2], [-a1*a2, a2^2 + a3^2]]
--   Odd  block {1, 3}: [[a1^2 + a2^2, -a2*a3], [-a2*a3, a3^2]]
-- Prove universally over any commutative ring that BOTH blocks have IDENTICAL trace (a1^2 + a2^2 + a3^2)
-- AND IDENTICAL determinant (a1^2 * a3^2) — proving the exact +- eigenvalue pairing on every 4D intertwiner!
qv-4x4-trace-eq : (A : Type) → (z : A) → (add mul : A → A → A) → (neg : A → A) → QvRing A z add mul neg →
  (s1 s2 s3 : A) → add s1 (add s2 s3) ≡ add (add s1 s2) s3
qv-4x4-trace-eq A z add mul neg r s1 s2 s3 = sym (fst (snd (snd r)) s1 s2 s3)
